omatically calculated. Alternatively, the processing extent and cell size of the output raster can be specified in the Environments tab of the Distance Accumulation tool.","position":{"start":{"line":16,"column":1},"end":{"line":16,"column":1}},"key":"BaoS1mVS5k"}],"key":"splSbqMePr"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note","key":"dEYFOJlkIr"}],"key":"OnCCMr9fx4"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The appropriate tool in QGIS is Proximity (raster distance) under GDAL. The input layer must be in raster format. Therefore, any points must first be converted to raster using Rasterize, defining the cell size and output extent. The Proximity Raster tool under SAGA has similar functionality.","position":{"start":{"line":19,"column":1},"end":{"line":19,"column":1}},"key":"uaQYMcPLZy"}],"key":"BfgTNxOWrD"}],"key":"IxtsmdQeMf"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that a similar visualization to that achieved with the Buffer or Multiple Ring Buffer tool can be achieved by changing the symbology of the distance accumulation raster, namely by changing the Stretch symbology to Classify in ArcGIS Pro.","position":{"start":{"line":22,"column":1},"end":{"line":22,"column":1}},"key":"JEEy4dxfi6"}],"key":"F1gbvUGyE5"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note","key":"HuKEjLYSY1"}],"key":"hzd1mFgMAX"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the Discrete symbology in QGIS.","position":{"start":{"line":25,"column":1},"end":{"line":25,"column":1}},"key":"tIBxNwHj6B"}],"key":"IuPu2Ib3XS"}],"key":"hQOjeVAwL7"},{"type":"image","url":"/distanceclass-a8f1bf3339f63e877c